A||||4||fyerstarter||ARGGH!!    Giving her gas kills her... PLEASE HELP!||||9||
Z||000000||fyerstarter||04-20-2001||11:04 PM||||So I'm driving home from work today and all of a sudden out of nowhere she just starts running like **** ! Whenever I give it some gas it starts cutting out and almost stalls or does stall. It seems to idle OK and doesnt really sound like it's missing but when you gas it major problems. I was able to limp her home and its raining and dark out right now so I can't look at it right now but any troubleshooting steps or suggestions would be tremendously appreciated.<P>Heres a little info:<P>-It's an 87 gt, 2.8<BR>-When it happened I did not get any check engine lights and still havent since<BR>-Occasionally when I am driving at freeway speeds I'll get a check engine light and they turned out to be codes 32, and 35<BR>-I have checked the vacuum lines and EGR tube and visually there appear to be no breaks or cracks<BR>-I replaced the fuel filter, plug wires, ignition module, dist cap, and coil about 2 months ago<BR>-There has been a bit of a knock in the engine for the past year that I have owned it which judging from what people told me here sounds like rod bearings going out<BR>-Up until today I have had no problems like this before<P>Any ideas? Thanks a million guys... and girls  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||9
Z||000001||WKDFIRO||04-20-2001||11:07 PM||||A code 35 is the Idle Air Control Valve, it might have gotten a little buggered up and just needs a shot of cleaner. But after that I would check the fuel preasure just to make sure you're okay there too!<P>Good luck!<p>[This message has been edited by WKDFIRO (edited 04-20-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000002||fyerstarter||04-20-2001||11:11 PM||||Thanks wkd, how would I check the fuel pressure? Also I live alone so this is going to be a one-man operation. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Seanh||04-21-2001||05:06 PM||||Check out, maybe replace, your MAP sensor. My connector broke and it came unplugged and runs excatly like your describing. I would punch the gas and the engine would just stay at idle speed like the throttle cable was off or somthing, then all the sudden it would jerk like crazy and take off again for a while.||||reg||1
Z||000004||WKDFIRO||04-22-2001||02:17 PM||||Connect a machanical fuel gauge to the fuel rail (you can see the fitting near the therm cap) and just check the preasures. According to the book it should read between 40.5 to 47lbs for the V6. I know there are more specific procedures to take the preasure reading its just been a while since Ive done it. I can't remember if the preasure remains the same when you start the engine. Hopefully someone here can fill in the spaces!<P>It is a one man operation so you shouldn't have any problems.<P>Good luck to you!||||reg||1
